hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1911","Narrated Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him): A boy was born to me, so I took him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He named him Ibrahim, chewed some dates and put it in his mouth (palate), and prayed for blessings for him, then handed him back to me."
"1912","The hadith of Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abdullah bin Zubair was born in the mosque of Quba. The hadith regarding migration has already been mentioned, and in this narration, it is further stated that the Muslims were very happy at his birth because people used to say to them that the Jews had cast a spell on you, therefore you would not have any children."
"1913","Sayyiduna Salman bin Amir Ad-Dabbi (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Aqiqah for a boy is (obligatory); shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."""
"1914","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""There is no (prescribed) practice of Fara’ and ‘Atirah in Islam."" Fara’ was the first offspring of a she-camel, which the polytheists used to slaughter in the name of their idols, and ‘Atirah was a kid goat that used to be sacrificed in the first ten days of Rajab."""
